--TEST--
`self` names the class it is written in and `parent` the one that class extends, so a `::` after either offers that class's static half although the access resolved to nothing yet — `rule:ide/an-accepted-type-writes-what-follows-it`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Base {
    public const int FLOOR = 1;
    public static function make(): Base { return new Base(); }
}

class Counter extends Base {
    public const int LIMIT = 10;
    public static int $count = 0;
    public function bump(): void {
        var $a = self::<|>
        if (true) {
        }
    }
}
